**Phase 3: Mobile App Packaging (1-2 Months After PWA)**

**Recommended: Capacitor (Cross-Platform)**
```bash
# Setup Capacitor in existing Vite project
npm install @capacitor/core @capacitor/cli
npx cap init

# Add platforms
npm install @capacitor/android @capacitor/ios
npx cap add android
npx cap add ios

# Build and sync
npm run build
npx cap sync
npx cap open android  # Opens Android Studio
npx cap open ios      # Opens Xcode (macOS only)

# Native plugins to add:
- @capacitor/push-notifications  # For push notifications
- @capacitor/share               # Native share functionality
- @capacitor/camera              # Camera access for uploads
- @capacitor/app                 # App lifecycle events
- @capacitor/status-bar          # Status bar styling
```

**Why Capacitor (NOT React Native):**
- ✅ Uses 100% of existing web codebase (no rewrite)
- ✅ Wraps your Vite/React app in native container
- ✅ Access to native features (push, camera, share)
- ✅ Single codebase for web, Android, iOS
- ✅ Can publish to Google Play + App Store
- ❌ React Native would require months of rebuilding entire app

**Alternative: TWA (Trusted Web Activity) - Android Only, Fastest MVP**
- Packages PWA as native Android app using Chrome Custom Tabs
- ~90% less work than full Capacitor setup
- Can publish to Google Play
- Best for quick Android-only launch
- Limitations: No native features, Android only

**Mobile App Action Items:**
1. ✅ Install Capacitor dependencies
2. ✅ Configure capacitor.config.json
3. ✅ Test on Android emulator
4. ✅ Test on real Android device
5. ✅ Prepare Google Play Store listing (screenshots, description, privacy policy)
6. ✅ Submit to Play Store (review time: 1-3 days)
7. ✅ iOS version after Android validated (requires macOS + $99/year Apple Developer account)

---

**Phase 4: App Store Optimization (Post-Launch)**
```
Google Play Store Requirements:
├── App name and description
├── Privacy policy URL (your-domain.com/privacy)
├── Terms of service URL (your-domain.com/terms)
├── App icon (512x512 PNG)
├── Feature graphic (1024x500)
├── Screenshots (phone + tablet)
├── Content rating questionnaire
├── Target age group
└── Domain verification (Search Console)

Apple App Store Requirements:
├── All above + App Preview video (optional but recommended)
├── Apple Developer Account ($99/year)
├── macOS with Xcode for builds
├── App Store Connect account
├── App Review Guidelines compliance
└── Privacy nutrition label
```

