#### 🔍 **ROOM GROUPS SYSTEM (Phase 2 Complete)** (May 6, 2026)
**Status:** ✅ COMPLETE - Discord-style chat segmentation with full UI integration

**Overview:**
Implemented a complete Discord-style groups system for room chat organization. Each room can now have multiple chat groups (channels) allowing hosts to segment conversations (e.g., "General", "Spoilers", "Memes", "VIP") while maintaining a single unified watch session. Includes image upload, member management modal, and context-aware header display.

**Phase 2 Updates (Latest - May 6, 2026):**
- ✅ **RoomGroupEditModal Component:** Full-featured modal with Details/Members/Settings tabs
- ✅ **Image Upload Support:** Groups can now have uploaded images (not just emojis)
- ✅ **Context-Aware Header:** Shows group name, image, and member count when viewing group
- ✅ **Conditional Action Buttons:** Begin Watch/Schedule/RoomTV only visible in main chat
- ✅ **Wider Sidebar:** Increased from w-16/20 to w-20/24 for better text visibility  
- ✅ **Member Management UI:** Add member icons, join/leave functionality, invite links
- ✅ **Right-Click to Edit:** Context menu on group icons opens edit modal
- ✅ **Mobile Support:** Group context properly displayed in mobile header
- ✅ **Fixed Backend Routes:** All use consistent `:id` parameter (not `:roomId`)

**Key Features:**
- **Discord-Style Sidebar:** Vertical channel list with image/emoji icons, tooltips, active state indicators (width: w-20/24)
- **Main Chat + Groups:** Default main chat (💬 with room image) + custom groups with uploaded images or emoji icons
- **Host Controls:** Create/edit/delete groups in Room Settings → Groups tab (emoji picker removed, image upload only)
- **Member Management:** Join/leave groups, view member lists with avatars/join dates, copy invite links
- **Smart Context Switching:** Header dynamically shows room OR group info (image, name, member count) based on `selectedGroupId`
- **Action Button Filtering:** Room-level actions (Begin Watch, Schedule, RoomTV) hidden when viewing groups
- **Image Upload:** Upload custom images for group icons (max 5MB, uses /api/rooms/:id/upload endpoint)
- **Delete Protection:** Confirmation required before deletion (in modal settings tab)
- **Delete Protection:** Double-click confirmation to prevent accidents

**Implementation Details:**

1. **Database Models (backend/internal/models/):**
   - `RoomGroup`: id, room_id, name, description, icon, created_by, is_public, display_order
   - `UserRoomGroup`: Junction table for many-to-many user-group membership
   - `RoomMessage.room_group_id`: Nullable FK for message filtering (null = main chat)

2. **Backend Handlers (backend/internal/handlers/room_groups.go - 486 lines):**
   - `CreateRoomGroupHandler`: Host creates groups with validation
   - `GetRoomGroupsHandler`: Lists groups with member counts
   - `UpdateRoomGroupHandler`: Host edits group properties
   - `DeleteRoomGroupHandler`: Host deletes groups (cascades to messages)
   - `JoinRoomGroupHandler`: Users join groups
   - `LeaveRoomGroupHandler`: Users leave groups
   - `GetRoomGroupMembersHandler`: Lists group members

3. **API Routes (7 endpoints registered in main.go):**
   ```go
   POST   /api/rooms/:roomId/groups              // Create group
   GET    /api/rooms/:roomId/groups              // List groups
   PUT    /api/rooms/:roomId/groups/:groupId     // Update group
   DELETE /api/rooms/:roomId/groups/:groupId     // Delete group
   POST   /api/rooms/:roomId/groups/:groupId/join    // Join group
   DELETE /api/rooms/:roomId/groups/:groupId/leave   // Leave group
   GET    /api/rooms/:roomId/groups/:groupId/members // Get members
   ```

4. **Message Filtering:**
   - `GET /api/rooms/:roomId/messages?room_group_id=123` → Group messages
   - `GET /api/rooms/:roomId/messages?room_group_id=null` → Main chat only
   - `GET /api/rooms/:roomId/messages` → All messages (no filter)
   - WebSocket broadcasts include `room_group_id` field

5. **Frontend Components:**
   - **RoomPageEditModal.jsx → Groups Tab:** Full CRUD UI with emoji picker (16 common emojis), name/description inputs, public/private toggle, inline editing, member counts
   - **RoomPageLeftSidebar.jsx (NEW - 114 lines):** Discord-style vertical sidebar with:
     - Main chat button (💬 icon)
     - Group buttons with custom emojis
     - Active state indicator (purple background + left border)
     - Hover tooltips with member counts
     - Delete button (host-only, double-click confirmation)
     - Conditional rendering (returns null if no groups)
   - **RoomPageNew.jsx Integration:**
     - **State:** 
       - `roomGroups`, `selectedGroupId`, `loadingGroups`
       - `isGroupEditModalOpen`, `selectedGroup`, `isUserGroupMember`
     - **Functions:** 
       - `fetchRoomGroups`, `handleGroupSelect`, `handleDeleteGroupFromSidebar`
       - `handleGroupEdit`, `handleGroupUpdate`, `handleGroupDelete`
       - `handleGroupJoin`, `handleGroupLeave`, `fetchMessagesForGroup`
     - **Header (Desktop & Mobile - Lines ~1890-2060):**
       - Dynamically shows group image when `selectedGroupId !== null`
       - Shows group name instead of room name when in group
       - Shows group member count instead of room member count
       - Hides host info when viewing group (only shows in main chat)
       - Uses `roomGroups.find(g => g.ID === selectedGroupId)` to get active group
     - **Conditional Actions (Lines ~1942-1990, ~2052-2116):**
       - Begin Watch, Schedule Event, RoomTV wrapped in `{!selectedGroupId && (...)}`
       - These buttons only appear in main chat, hidden in group chats
       - Prevents confusion (can't start watch sessions from group chats)
     - **Layout:** Flex container with RoomPageLeftSidebar + chat area
     - **Message sending:** Includes `room_group_id` in WebSocket payload
     - **WebSocket filtering:** Only displays messages matching `selectedGroupId`
     - **Modal Integration:** Renders RoomGroupEditModal with all necessary props

6. **User Flow:**
   - **Creating Groups:**
     - Host opens Room Settings → Groups tab
     - Clicks "Create New Group" (only visible to host)
     - Uploads image or keeps emoji, enters name/description
     - Group appears in sidebar automatically
   - **Navigating Groups:**
     - Click group icon in sidebar → switches to that group
     - Header updates to show group image, name, member count
     - Begin Watch/Schedule/RoomTV buttons disappear
     - Chat only shows messages for that group
   - **Managing Groups:**
     - Right-click group icon OR click group name → opens RoomGroupEditModal
     - Non-members: See join button in Details tab
     - Members: See leave button, can view Members tab
     - Host: Can edit all details, view members, delete in Settings tab
   - **Messaging:**
     - Send message → includes current `room_group_id`
     - Messages only visible when that group is selected
     - Switch back to main chat → see main room messages

**Technical Architecture:**
- **Phase 1 (✅):** Room sorting, backend endpoints, database models
- **Phase 2 (✅):** Complete UI integration, image upload, member management, context-aware display
- **Phase 3 (Planned):** Follow system + 1-room-per-creator limit

**API Client (frontend/src/services/api.js - Lines 607-641):**
```javascript
export const createRoomGroup = async (roomId, groupData) // POST with icon URL
export const getRoomGroups = async (roomId)              // GET with member_count
export const updateRoomGroup = async (roomId, groupId, groupData) // PUT
export const deleteRoomGroup = async (roomId, groupId)   // DELETE
export const joinRoomGroup = async (roomId, groupId)     // POST
export const leaveRoomGroup = async (roomId, groupId)    // POST (not DELETE)
export const getRoomGroupMembers = async (roomId, groupId) // GET with user details
```

**Dependencies Installed:**
- `@headlessui/react@^2.2.0` - Modal component library (Dialog, Transition) for RoomGroupEditModal
- Installed via: `npm install @headlessui/react`

**Bug Fixes:**
- ✅ Fixed 400 Bad Request on `/api/rooms/108/groups` - Changed handlers to use global `DB` variable instead of `c.MustGet("db")`
- ✅ Fixed route parameter inconsistency - All routes now use `:id` instead of mixed `:roomId`/:id`
- ✅ Fixed image upload in edit modal - Properly initializes `imagePreview` from group icon URL
- ✅ Fixed duplicate code causing syntax errors during implementation
- ✅ Backend server restarted successfully after route fixes

**Why This Matters:**
Previously, creators needed multiple rooms to segment audiences (spoiler-free vs spoilers, members vs VIP, etc.), causing fragmentation. Now they can organize all conversations in ONE room with focused channels, similar to Discord servers. The context-aware UI ensures users always know which group they're in (header shows group info), and conditional action buttons prevent confusion (can't start watch sessions from group chats). Image upload support allows for professional branding of groups beyond simple emojis.

