## 🔐 SECURITY & AUTHENTICATION (LATEST: April 25, 2026)

### **Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) System:**
- **TOTP Implementation**: Google Authenticator compatible (30-second codes, SHA1 algorithm)
- **QR Code Generation**: External API (qrserver.com) for easy device setup
- **Backup Codes**: 10 one-time recovery codes (8 characters each) for account recovery
- **Security Events**: All 2FA actions logged (setup, enable, disable, failed attempts)
- **Database Fields**: `User.TwoFactorSecret`, `TwoFactorEnabled`, `BackupCodes`, `LastLoginIP`

### **Security Settings UI (LobbyLeftSidebar):**
- **SecurityModal Component**: Two-tab interface
  - **2FA Tab**: Setup wizard (password verification → QR display → backup codes → TOTP verification)
  - **Change Password Tab**: Current password verification + new password confirmation
- **Security Badge**: Shows "2FA ✓" when enabled, purple gradient highlight when disabled
- **Real-time Status**: ACTIVE/INACTIVE indicators with color coding

### **API Endpoints:**
- `POST /api/auth/setup-2fa` - Generate QR code and backup codes
- `POST /api/auth/verify-2fa-setup` - Enable 2FA after TOTP verification
- `POST /api/auth/disable-2fa` - Disable 2FA (requires password + current code)
- `POST /api/auth/change-password` - Update password with security logging
- `POST /api/auth/login` - Extended to check 2FA status and validate codes

### **Documentation:**
