### **🔐 Security Status (April 23, 2026):**

**✅ IMPLEMENTED SECURITY MEASURES:**
- **Password Hashing**: bcrypt with cost factor 12 (strong)
- **JWT Authentication**: 64-char secret, 24-hour token expiry, HS256 signing
- **Rate Limiting**: Auth endpoints limited to 5 attempts/minute per IP
- **Database SSL**: Conditional SSL (required for Railway production, disabled for local dev)
- **Age Verification**: COPPA compliance (13+ years old requirement)
- **Token Storage**: JWT in localStorage, WebSocket token in sessionStorage
- **Environment Variables**: .env in .gitignore, secrets not committed to Git
- **API Key Protection**: All payment/SMTP keys stored in environment variables

**⚠️ KNOWN SECURITY GAPS (Post-Launch Priority):**
- No CORS whitelist (currently allows all origins with patterns - allows localhost, Vercel, Cloudflare Tunnel)
- No session invalidation on logout (JWT remains valid until 24h expiry)
- No account lockout after failed login attempts (rate limiting exists but no permanent lockout)
- No 2FA/MFA option for sensitive actions (withdrawals, password changes)
- No SQL query logging for audit trail (GORM protects against SQL injection, admin actions now audited)
- No Content Security Policy (CSP) headers (XSS protection not enforced)
- No automated dependency vulnerability scanning (no CI/CD security checks)

**🎯 POST-LAUNCH SECURITY ROADMAP:**
- **Week 1**: Implement CORS whitelist, add logout token blacklist
- **Week 2**: ~~Add account lockout (5 failed attempts)~~, ~~SQL audit logging~~ ✅ Admin audit logging implemented
- **Week 3**: Implement CSP headers, dependency scanning (npm audit, go list)
- **Month 2**: Add 2FA option (SMS/email), encrypt sensitive payment data
- **Month 3**: Security audit, penetration testing

