## 🎯 RECENT FEATURE IMPLEMENTATIONS (April 24, 2026)

### **1. 3D Cinema LiveShare Audio Enhancements**

#### Auto-Enable Host Broadcasting
**File**: `frontend/src/components/cinema/3d-cinema/CinemaScene3DDemo.jsx`

**Implementation Details:**
- When host starts LiveShare, `isHostBroadcasting` automatically enables
- When host ends LiveShare, `isHostBroadcasting` automatically disables
- State persists across component lifecycle using `previousDiscussionModeRef`

**Code Locations:**
- **Line 5320-5324**: `handleLiveShareModeSelect` - Auto-enables host broadcasting
  ```javascript
  // ✅ AUTO-ENABLE HOST BROADCASTING when LiveShare starts
  if (isHost) {
    setIsHostBroadcasting(true);
    console.log('🎤 [LiveShare] Auto-enabled host broadcasting');
  }
  ```

- **Line 5258-5265**: `handleEndLiveShare` - Auto-disables host broadcasting
  ```javascript
  // ✅ AUTO-DISABLE HOST BROADCASTING when LiveShare ends
  if (isHost && isHostBroadcasting) {
    setIsHostBroadcasting(false);
    console.log('🎤 [LiveShare] Auto-disabled host broadcasting');
  }
  ```

#### Asymmetric Audio Routing
**Purpose**: Host broadcasts to all theaters but only hears their own row (prevents echo/feedback from 100+ participants)

**Code Location:**
- **Line 2161-2218**: `shouldSubscribeToSpeaker` function
  ```javascript
  const shouldSubscribeToSpeaker = (speakerUserId) => {
    // Host broadcasting to everyone - subscribe if you're not the host
    if (speakerState[speakerUserId]?.isHostBroadcasting && speakerUserId !== currentUser?.id) {
      return true;
    }
    
    // Host hears only their own theater/row (asymmetric audio)
    if (isHost && userSeats[speakerUserId]) {
      const speakerTheater = userSeats[speakerUserId].theaterNumber;
      const speakerRow = userSeats[speakerUserId].seatRow;
      const myTheater = userSeats[currentUser.id]?.theaterNumber || 1;
      const myRow = userSeats[currentUser.id]?.seatRow;
      
      return speakerTheater === myTheater && speakerRow === myRow;
    }
    
    // Regular seat-based audio routing for non-hosts
    // ... (existing logic)
  };
  ```

**Theater System Architecture:**
- All theaters share same `session_id` (same video content)
- Each theater isolated by `theaterNumber` in seat assignments
- LiveKit room uses session-based naming, not theater-based
- Audio routing handled by `shouldSubscribeToSpeaker` logic
- Host broadcasting transcends theater boundaries (all theaters hear host)
- Regular seat mode: Audio isolated per theater/row/column

